IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch5.l4 (Schedule 5, paragraphs A1 to 3B). Every expected value is written by hand from the text,
-- beside the assertion; none is copied from the encoding's output. Deontic traces are run with #TRACE and read by eye
-- (the stable binary prints their outcome but offers no assertion on it): see NOTES.md.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 5 paragraphs A1 to 3B`

§§ `Fixtures`

`sch 5 test twelve months exactly` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025
`sch 5 test a day short of twelve months` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 12 2025
`sch 5 test six months` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 6 2025
`sch 5 test mid-month twelve months` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 15 3 2024, `the last day` IS Date 14 3 2025
`sch 5 test mid-month one day short` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 15 3 2024, `the last day` IS Date 13 3 2025
`sch 5 test leap day start, 26 February` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 29 2 2024, `the last day` IS Date 26 2 2025
`sch 5 test leap day start, 27 February` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 29 2 2024, `the last day` IS Date 27 2 2025
`sch 5 test leap day start, 28 February` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 29 2 2024, `the last day` IS Date 28 2 2025
`sch 5 test leap day start, 1 March` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 29 2 2024, `the last day` IS Date 1 3 2025
`sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 3 2025

§§ `A1(1) -- 12 months`

-- Expected: 1 Jan 2025 to 31 Dec 2025 is exactly 12 months (true); to 30 Dec 2025 is a day short (false).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test a day short of twelve months` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test six months` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Expected: 15 Mar 2024 to 14 Mar 2025 is 12 months; to 13 Mar 2025 is not.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test mid-month twelve months` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test mid-month one day short` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Expected (fork F1): a deferment from 29 Feb 2024 is under 12 months on 26 Feb 2025 on both readings, over on 28 Feb and 1 Mar,
-- and the two readings differ only on 27 Feb 2025, which is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test leap day start, 26 February` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test leap day start, 27 February` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test leap day start, 28 February` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` `sch 5 test leap day start, 1 March` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `A1(1) -- the duty`

-- Expected: deferred and 12 months: the person must elect (true). Under 12 months, or not deferred: the sub-paragraph does not
-- speak (NOTHING). The leap-day fork day is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5 test a day short of twelve months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` FALSE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(1) the person must elect` TRUE `sch 5 test leap day start, 27 February` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative duty. The prescribed period is 28 days here (an input). Read by eye:
--   an election on day 10 -> FULFILLED; a lapse to day 29 with no election -> FULFILLED (A1(2) deems the lump sum election).
#TRACE `sch 5 para A1(1) the election duty` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 5 the person whose entitlement is deferred` DOES `sch 5 makes an election` `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies` AT 10
#TRACE `sch 5 para A1(1) the election duty` 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)

§§ `A1(2) -- no election in time`

-- Expected: no election in time -> treated as the (b) lump-sum election; an election made stands.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made` NOTHING EQUALS `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(2) the election that is treated as made` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`

§§ `A1(4) -- the part of the pension an election does not touch`

-- Expected: weekly rate 150 of which 10 is an increase under paragraphs 5 to 6A: the election applies to 140.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(4) the weekly rate to which an election applies` 150 10 EQUALS 140
#ASSERT `sch 5 para A1(4) the weekly rate to which an election applies` 150 0 EQUALS 150

§§ `Paragraph 1(1) -- when the increase paragraph applies`

-- Expected: under 12 months -> applies (a). 12 months and an increase election -> applies (b). 12 months and a lump-sum election, or no election
-- -> NOTHING (neither condition). Not deferred -> NOTHING. The leap-day fork day -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE `sch 5 test leap day start, 27 February` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 1(2) -- the 1 per cent floor`

-- Expected: rate 100: an aggregate of 1.00 is exactly 1 per cent (increase 1.00); 0.99 is not enough (increase 0); 2.50 is (2.50).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 1 100 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 0.99 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 2.5 100 EQUALS 2.5

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- increments`

-- 2(2): six days of increment make one complete incremental period. Expected: 12 -> 2, 11 -> 1, 6 -> 1, 5 -> 0, 0 -> 0.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` 12 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` 11 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` 6 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` 5 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(2) the number of complete incremental periods` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(1) the number of increments` 4 EQUALS 4
-- 2(4) rounding to the nearest penny, 1/2p going up; under 1/2p is zero. Expected by hand:
-- 0.004 -> 0; 0.005 -> 0.01; 1.234 -> 1.23; 1.235 -> 1.24; 1.2349 -> 1.23.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` 0.004 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` 0.005 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` 1.234 EQUALS 1.23
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` 1.235 EQUALS 1.24
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(4) the amount calculated under sub-paragraph (3) as rounded` 1.2349 EQUALS 1.23
-- 2(3): 1/5th per cent of the weekly rate, rounded. Rate 100 -> 0.2; rate 122.5 -> 0.245 -> 0.25 (half up); rate 122 -> 0.244 -> 0.24.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` 100 EQUALS 0.2
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` 122.5 EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` 122 EQUALS 0.24
-- Rate 184.90 -> 0.3698 before rounding; 2(4)(a) (src:5090) rounds it to the nearest penny, so the increment is 0.37.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(3) the increment for one incremental period` 184.9 EQUALS 0.37
-- Paragraph 2 aggregate: rate 122.5, 12 days = 2 periods x 0.25 = 0.5; rate 100, 18 days = 3 periods x 0.2 = 0.6; 5 days = 0.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2 the aggregate of the increments` 122.5 12 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2 the aggregate of the increments` 100 18 EQUALS 0.6
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2 the aggregate of the increments` 100 5 EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph 2(5) to (8) -- what the weekly rate counts`

`sch 5 test a pension with every named increase` MEANS `sch 5 Weekly pension` WITH
    `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule` IS 100
    `the increase under section 47(1)` IS 5
    `the increase under paragraph 4` IS 3
    `the increases under paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS 2
    `the increase under section 83A` IS 7
    `the increase under section 85` IS 11
    `the graduated retirement benefit` IS 13

`sch 5 test a plain pension` MEANS `sch 5 Weekly pension` WITH
    `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule` IS 50
    `the increase under section 47(1)` IS 0
    `the increase under paragraph 4` IS 0
    `the increases under paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS 0
    `the increase under section 83A` IS 0
    `the increase under section 85` IS 0
    `the graduated retirement benefit` IS 0

-- Expected: 100 + 5 (47(1)) + 3 (para 4) + 2 (paras 5 to 6A) = 110; the 83A (7), 85 (11) and graduated (13) amounts are left out.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(5) the weekly rate of pension for sub-paragraph (3)` `sch 5 test a pension with every named increase` EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(5) the weekly rate of pension for sub-paragraph (3)` `sch 5 test a plain pension` EQUALS 50
-- 2(6): the section 47(1) increase counted is the one before the section 47(2) deduction: 12, whatever is payable after it (4).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(6) the increase under section 47(1) that is counted` 12 4 EQUALS 12
-- 2(7): an order during the deferment -> the rate as if in force before it began (110); no order -> not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(7) the rate for an incremental period` TRUE 100 110 EQUALS JUST 110
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(7) the rate for an incremental period` FALSE 100 110 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2(8): premium paid and increment after it: 100 - 8 = 92; premium not paid, or increment before it: not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(8) the weekly rate used for an increment` TRUE TRUE 100 8 EQUALS JUST 92
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(8) the weekly rate used for an increment` FALSE TRUE 100 8 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2(8) the weekly rate used for an increment` TRUE FALSE 100 8 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraphs 1 and 2 together`

-- Under 12 months, no election, rate 200, 24 days of increment: 4 periods x 0.4 = 1.6, below 1 per cent of 200 (2.00): increase 0.
-- 29 days: 4 periods = 1.6 -> 0. 30 days: 5 periods x 0.4 = 2.0, exactly 1 per cent: increase 2. 60 days: 10 x 0.4 = 4.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING 200 24 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING 200 29 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING 200 30 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test six months` NOTHING 200 60 EQUALS JUST 4
-- 12 months and an increase election: the same sums apply; 12 months and a lump-sum election: paragraph 1 does not apply (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`) 200 60 EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 1 the amount by which the pension is increased for the deferment` TRUE `sch 5 test twelve months exactly` (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) 200 60 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 2A`

-- Expected: applies only with the pension including a paragraph 5 to 6A increase and the lump-sum election; otherwise NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2A(3): 1/5th per cent of the weekly increase, no rounding: 10 -> 0.02; 12.5 -> 0.025. 2A(2): 3 periods of a rate-10 increase -> 0.06.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(3) the increment for one incremental period` 10 EQUALS 0.02
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(3) the increment for one incremental period` 12.5 EQUALS 0.025
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 10 3 EQUALS 0.06
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 2A(2) the amount by which the rate of the pension is increased` 10 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph 3A`

-- Expected: deferred and the lump-sum election -> entitled; the increase election or no deferment -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` TRUE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` TRUE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 1 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` FALSE (JUST `sch 5 an election that paragraph 3A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3A(2) the person is entitled to a lump sum` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3B -- the lump sum`

-- Prescribed day Monday (1). 1 Jan 2025 is a Wednesday, so 6 Jan 2025 is the first Monday; 31 Mar 2025 is also a Monday.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 31 3 2025) 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 7 1 2025) 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 30 12 2024) 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 5 para 3B(2) an accrual period begins on the day` (Date 7 4 2025) 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025`)
-- The last accrual period: deferment ending on Monday 31 Mar 2025 -> 31 Mar to 6 Apr 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` 1 `sch 5 test the first quarter of 2025` EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 31 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 6 4 2025)
-- Deferment 1 Jan to 30 Mar 2025 (Sunday): the last Monday is 24 Mar -> 24 to 30 Mar 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` 1 (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 24 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 30 3 2025)
-- Deferment 1 to 3 Jan 2025 (Wednesday to Friday): no Monday falls in it -> not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` 1 (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3B(3): the formula is omitted from the text, so the accrued amount is not covered whatever A, P and R are.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` 0 100 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` 50 120 6 EQUALS NOTHING
-- R: base rate 4 and no prescription -> 6 (two points higher). A prescribed 7 is higher than 6 -> 7. A prescribed 6 or 5 is not "higher" -> not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` 4 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` 4 (JUST 7) EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` 4 (JUST 6) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` 4 (JUST 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3B(4): a change on Wednesday 8 Jan 2025 (in the period that began Monday 6 Jan) takes effect Monday 13 Jan 2025;
-- a change on Monday 13 Jan 2025 takes effect 20 Jan 2025; prescribed other time 15 Jan 2025 prevails if regulations so provide.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` (Date 8 1 2025) 1 NOTHING EQUALS Date 13 1 2025
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` (Date 13 1 2025) 1 NOTHING EQUALS Date 20 1 2025
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` (Date 8 1 2025) 1 (JUST (Date 15 1 2025)) EQUALS Date 15 1 2025
-- 3B(5): 100 + 5 (47(1)) + 3 (para 4) - 4 (prescribed to be left out) = 104; paragraphs 5 to 6A (2), 83A (7), 85 (11), graduated (13) are not counted.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` `sch 5 test a pension with every named increase` 4 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` `sch 5 test a plain pension` 0 EQUALS 50
-- 3B(1): the lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period; no accrued amount, no lump sum.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(1) the lump sum before rounding` (JUST 12.345) EQUALS JUST 12.345
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3B(1) the lump sum before rounding` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
